PROGRAM IMPLEMENTATION

Drawing System

Freehand drawing uses three mouse events on the Tkinter Canvas. Pressing the left mouse button calls start_drawing, which records the starting point and saves a copy of the current image for undo. Moving the mouse calls draw_motion, which draws a line on the Pillow image from the previous point to the current point using ImageDraw. Releasing the button calls finish_drawing, which ends the stroke. One complete press-drag-release is stored as one undoable action, not every tiny movement.

Color Selection

The Choose Color button opens the system color chooser through colorchooser.askcolor. When a color is selected, set_color updates the active drawing color and changes the color indicator label. The six quick color buttons also call set_color with preset colors. Changing colors never changes the brush size.

Brush Size

A horizontal Scale widget lets the user choose any brush size from 1 to 100. The change_brush_size function converts the slider value to an integer and updates the size label and status bar immediately. The value is used as the width of freehand lines and shape outlines.

Eraser Tool

Selecting the Eraser tool switches the active tool to eraser. The paint_color function then returns white instead of the chosen color, so drawing with the eraser paints white pixels on the Pillow image. Because the saved file comes from that same Pillow image, erased areas are also white in the saved picture.

Shape Tools

The Line, Rectangle, Oval, and Triangle tools all work by dragging from a starting point to an ending point. While the mouse moves, preview_shape_drawing draws a temporary outline or fill on the Tkinter Canvas using the preview tag. When the mouse is released, the preview is deleted and draw_final_shape draws the permanent shape into the Pillow image. Rectangles, ovals, and triangles can be filled when the Fill Shapes checkbox is selected. The triangle is built from three points: the top middle, bottom left, and bottom right of the drag box.

Undo Function

The program keeps a history list of Pillow image copies. Before every action, push_history stores the current image state. The undo function removes the most recent saved state and restores it to the canvas. This reverses one complete stroke, one shape, a clear operation, or an opened image. The history is limited to 50 states to keep memory use reasonable.

Clear Canvas

The Clear button calls clear_canvas, which first displays a Yes or No confirmation dialog asking whether the entire canvas should be cleared. If the user chooses No, nothing happens. If the user chooses Yes, the current image is saved to history, a white rectangle is drawn over the whole Pillow image, and the canvas is refreshed.

Open and Save Image

The Open button uses filedialog.askopenfilename to select a PNG, JPG, JPEG, or BMP file. The image is converted to RGB, resized to fit inside the fixed canvas while keeping its proportions, centered on a white background of the required canvas size, and then displayed. Drawing can continue on the opened image. The Save button uses filedialog.asksaveasfilename and saves the actual Pillow image as PNG, JPEG, or BMP. A success message appears after saving, and errors are shown with messagebox.

Pillow Integration

Pillow is the image engine of the application. Image creates and stores the white canvas image. ImageDraw performs all drawing operations such as lines, ellipses, rectangles, polygons, and fills. ImageTk converts the Pillow image into a form the Tkinter Canvas can display. The refresh_canvas function keeps the Tkinter view and the Pillow image synchronized after every change.

FUNCTIONS USED

clamp_point: Keeps mouse coordinates inside the canvas boundaries.
paint_color: Returns white for the eraser and the chosen color for all other tools.
push_history: Saves the current image before an action so Undo can restore it.
refresh_canvas: Converts the Pillow image with ImageTk and displays it on the Canvas.
update_status: Updates the status bar with the current tool, color, size, and fill state.
make_button: Creates consistently styled buttons for the toolbar.
choose_color: Opens the system color picker.
set_color: Changes the active color and updates the color indicator.
set_tool: Selects a tool and highlights its button.
change_brush_size: Updates brush thickness from the 1 to 100 slider.
toggle_fill: Turns filled shapes on or off.
start_drawing: Begins a stroke or shape and records history.
draw_motion: Draws freehand lines or shows the shape preview.
finish_drawing: Ends a stroke or commits the final shape.
triangle_points: Calculates the three corners of the triangle.
preview_shape_drawing: Draws the temporary shape while dragging.
draw_final_shape: Draws the permanent shape into the Pillow image.
undo: Restores the previous image state.
clear_canvas: Asks for confirmation and then blanks the canvas.
open_image: Loads and fits an external image onto the canvas.
save_image: Saves the Pillow image to a file.
section: Creates a labeled toolbar section.

